["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Quail live in a narrow band: low, brushy, close to food and water, often next to people. Chukar live on the rock above them. Learn the band and you stop walking empty country.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cross section of a South Okanagan valley side from the lake up to the pine. Riparian brush by the lake and orchard edges: quail. Brushy draws on the lower benches: quail. Farm benches and stubble: maybe gray partridge. Steep rock and cheatgrass slopes: chukar. Open pine above: few quail. Quail breed mostly from 250 to 500 metres and rarely above 750 metres, BC Breeding Bird Atlas, 85 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Valley cross section: who lives where</text>\n<path d=\"M0 250 L60 250 L90 236 L150 232 L190 210 L240 200 L270 150 L300 110 L330 90 L400 70 L400 270 L0 270 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"244\" width=\"58\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"28\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">lake</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"78\" cy=\"238\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"170\" cy=\"214\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g fill=\"#3f7f3a\"><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"226\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"128\" cy=\"225\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"146\" cy=\"224\" r=\"7\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M270 150 l10 -6 l8 4 l-6 8 Z M296 116 l9 -5 l7 3 l-5 7 Z\" fill=\"#9a8f80\"/>\n<g fill=\"#556b2f\"><path d=\"M345 86 l8 -22 l8 22 Z\"/><path d=\"M372 78 l8 -22 l8 22 Z\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(84 222) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(172 198) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(286 134) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#b9a88a\"/><path d=\"M-20 -2 L-30 -4 L-28 5 Z\" fill=\"#8b6f4a\"/><path d=\"M-8 -6 v12 M-3 -7 v13 M2 -7 v13 M7 -6 v12\" stroke=\"#2f2f2f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9fa4a8\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 q6 -2 13 2 q-4 10 -11 10\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"#f3ead8\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"-15\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M26 -14 l5 1 l-5 3 Z\" fill=\"#d23b2a\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 8 M9 13 l2 8\" stroke=\"#d23b2a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(225 190) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">riparian</text>\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">QUAIL</text>\n<text x=\"128\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">orchard</text>\n<text x=\"175\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">brushy draw</text>\n<text x=\"225\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Huns?</text>\n<text x=\"240\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">CHUKAR</text>\n<text x=\"258\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">rock + cheatgrass</text>\n<text x=\"370\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pine</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"272\" width=\"380\" height=\"24\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail: mostly 250 to 500 m (85%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Quail: valley floor and first benches, brush beside food <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Chukar: steep rock and cheatgrass slopes above <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: habitat in full</summary><ul><li>BC: quail mostly breed below 750 m, most common from 250 to 500 m, some as high as 1,250 m (85%, BC Breeding Bird Atlas).</li><li>They prefer the Ponderosa Pine and Bunchgrass zones in the Interior <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Habitat: mixed farm and suburban areas with lots of cover for feeding, nesting and roosting, plus riparian, grassland and open pine or broadleaf woods <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>They need \"a mosaic of low, brushy vegetation, with grass and forb openings, taller shrubs, and trees, interspersed with water\" (80%, California habitat records).</li><li>Washington lists: thick tangles near stream beds, small ponds and wetlands; valley bottoms with Russian olive or tall sage; tree lines and fence lines; low brush and tall grass; edges of grain fields <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Chukar: open, rocky, dry slopes and canyon walls, usually steep; grass and brush cover with cheatgrass a key plant (75 to 80%, Audubon and FEIS).</li><li>Huns: cultivated land, hedgerows, bushy pastures and stubble (75%, Audubon).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-woods-rose-slope.jpg\" alt=\"Wild rose along a dry creek: thorny hiding cover.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Wild rose along a dry creek: thorny hiding cover. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rosa_woodsii_along_Douglas_Creek,_Douglas_County_Washington.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-blackberry.jpg\" alt=\"Blackberry thicket: a covey can vanish in it.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Blackberry thicket: a covey can vanish in it. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rubus_armeniacus_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-chokecherry.jpg\" alt=\"Chokecherry in fruit: brushy draws with berries.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Chokecherry in fruit: brushy draws with berries. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prunus_virginiana_fruittwo-9-08-04.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-snowberry.jpg\" alt=\"Snowberry: berries hang on into winter.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Snowberry: berries hang on into winter. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: NPS Photo, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:File-Symphoricarpos_albus_-_native;-Blooms_June_-_July;_(9352ce2f-155d-4519-3e7c-5033029f6900).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Thorny brush beside open feeding ground (Tip).</li><li>Food: seeds and green leaves, legumes first <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: foods by season</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th>Main food (80%, California records)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fall and winter</td><td>Seeds, waste grain, some fruit</td></tr><tr><td>Spring</td><td>Green leaves, new shoots, flowers</td></tr><tr><td>Summer</td><td>Seeds; chicks eat many insects</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Adults eat mostly seeds and green plants; legume seeds lead <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Insects are under 5% of the adult diet <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Also acorns, berries, flowers and bulbs (75%, Audubon).</li><li>In BC yards they take garden seed and sprouting peas (65%, BC Outdoors).</li><li>Plant names for the Okanagan draws are from the app's <a href=\"#/s/habitat-upland\">habitat tour</a>: rose, blackberry, chokecherry, snowberry (Tip for which ones hold birds).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-kamloops-sagebrush.jpg\" alt=\"Sagebrush slope near Kamloops: bare soil between grey shrubs.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Sagebrush slope near Kamloops: bare soil between grey shrubs. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Ghune, CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grassland.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-bitterbrush-slope.jpg\" alt=\"Bitterbrush on a dry slope: chukar country shrub.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Bitterbrush on a dry slope: chukar country shrub. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Pacific Southwest Region, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blooming_shrubs_on_hiking_trail_in_Nevada_(49867903218).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-lac-du-bois-grassland.jpg\" alt=\"Open bunchgrass in October.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Open bunchgrass in October. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: tuchodi, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lac_du_Bois_Grasslands_Protected_Area_(4043429977).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li>Steep, rocky, dry, with cheatgrass and sage (75 to 80%).</li><li>Water within reach in dry weather <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: chukar ground in full</summary><ul><li>The chukar's key plant in North America is cheatgrass (80%, FEIS). Also sagebrush, bitterbrush, currant and rabbitbrush slopes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Slopes are usually steep: over 7% grade with at least 60 m (200 ft) of rise <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Chukar need water unless they can eat lots of green leaves (75%, Audubon). Broods in California stay within about 3.2 km of water <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>BC: best on low slopes of the Thompson from Kamloops to Lytton; also in the South Okanagan and Similkameen (65%, BC Outdoors).</li><li>The quick lesson: mostly 250 to 500 m in the Thompson <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>; start at springs and creek mouths below cliffs (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Chart of elevation by month. California quail stay in a band from about 250 to 750 metres all year with no migration, BC atlas and the app migration data, 60 to 85 percent. A dashed chukar line drops lower in midwinter: chukar move down to lower ground in heavy snow, US Forest Service FEIS, 80 percent. The chukar line is a sketch; there are no BC numbers.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Elevation by month (general pattern)</text>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"70\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"66\" y1=\"220.0\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"220.0\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"62\" y=\"225.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">250 m</text>\n<line x1=\"66\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"170.0\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"62\" y=\"175.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">500 m</text>\n<line x1=\"66\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"62\" y=\"125.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">750 m</text>\n<line x1=\"66\" y1=\"70.0\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#d8d2c4\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"62\" y=\"75.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">1000 m</text>\n<text x=\"84.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<text x=\"109.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">F</text>\n<text x=\"135.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text>\n<text x=\"160.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n<text x=\"186.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text>\n<text x=\"211.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<text x=\"237.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">J</text>\n<text x=\"262.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text>\n<text x=\"288.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S</text>\n<text x=\"313.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">O</text>\n<text x=\"339.0\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">N</text>\n<text x=\"364.5\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">D</text>\n<rect x=\"72\" y=\"120.0\" width=\"312\" height=\"100.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".35\"/>\n<text x=\"228\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">California quail: 250 to 750 m all year</text>\n<text x=\"228\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(no migration, 60 to 85%)</text>\n<path d=\"M72 130 L150 128 L220 100 L300 110 L384 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#a33b2a\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"9 6\"/>\n<text x=\"384\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"end\">chukar: lower in deep snow</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chukar line: a sketch, no BC data (FEIS 80%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Quail: about 250 to 750 m all year. No migration (60 to 85%).</li><li>Chukar: move lower in deep snow <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: elevation in full</summary><ul><li>The app migration data puts quail at 250 to 750 m in every month, in Bunchgrass and Ponderosa Pine zones (60 to 75% by month).</li><li>Most BC breeding birds sit at 250 to 500 m <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Snow pushes quail lower and closer to houses (Tip, from the trip plan).</li><li>Chukar: altitudinal moves from higher to lower ground in heavy snow (80%, FEIS). No BC elevation numbers found by month: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Quail and chukar by region. Region 8, Okanagan: quail open 1 October to 30 November, chukar open the same dates. Region 3, Heffley Creek: no quail season at all, chukar open 1 October to 30 November.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"188\" height=\"284\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"8\" width=\"188\" height=\"284\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#efe2d6\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Region 8</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Okanagan</text>\n  <text x=\"298\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Region 3</text><text x=\"298\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heffley Creek</text>\n  <rect x=\"24\" y=\"80\" width=\"156\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail open</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct 1 to Nov 30</text>\n  <rect x=\"220\" y=\"80\" width=\"156\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><text x=\"298\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No quail</text><text x=\"298\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">no season (95%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"24\" y=\"170\" width=\"156\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chukar open</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct 1 to Nov 30</text>\n  <rect x=\"220\" y=\"170\" width=\"156\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"298\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Chukar open</text><text x=\"298\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct 1 to Nov 30</text>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">page 68 (99%)</text><text x=\"298\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">page 34 (99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>South Okanagan (Region 8): quail, chukar and Huns, all open <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Heffley Creek (Region 3): no quail row. Mission (Region 2): no quail row <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">97%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: each area in full</summary><ul><li>Region 8: quail, chukar, gray partridge and pheasant cocks have seasons in MUs (Management Units) 8-1 to 8-15 and 8-21 to 8-26 (99%, Rule Book).</li><li>Region 3, Heffley Creek: chukar and gray partridge rows in MUs 3-12 to 3-20 and 3-26 to 3-44, but <strong>no quail row</strong> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">97%</span>. Quail at the property are not legal game. Heffley Creek is outside the main quail range <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Region 2, Mission: pheasant cocks only, MUs 2-4 and 2-8; no quail, chukar or partridge rows <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">97%</span>. The Fraser Valley quail population appears gone anyway (85%, BC atlas).</li><li>Chukar near Heffley Creek: the dry Thompson valley slopes toward Lytton hold the best birds (65 to 75%).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Town</th><th>MU (Management Unit)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Osoyoos, Oliver, Vaseux Lake</td><td>8-1</td></tr><tr><td>Okanagan Falls, Kaleden</td><td>Meeting point of 8-1, 8-8 and 8-9</td></tr><tr><td>Penticton</td><td>On the 8-8 and 8-9 line. Naramata 8-9</td></tr><tr><td>Summerland, Peachland</td><td>8-8</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Read from the page 66 map (80 to 90%). Confirm on the official MU map.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more on the South Okanagan</summary><ul><li>Table copied from the <a href=\"#/s/local-okanagan\">Okanagan trip plan</a>: \"Read from the page 66 map and the map captions J1 to J18 (80 to 90%, Kelowna is the least certain).\"</li><li>Every quail MU on this list is open 1 October to 30 November <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Most South Okanagan quail sit on private land: valley farms, orchards and town edges (Tip, 75% from the trip plan).</li><li>No Shooting Areas, the Vaseux sanctuary and town bylaws are in chapter 9 and in the <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8 Rule Book</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stack of Hunt Map layer cards for a quail trip. California quail habitat, 60 percent general pattern. Private land: ask first. City and town limits: bylaws. Reserves: permission from the Nation. Parks and protected areas. Wildlife Management Areas. Management Units. Download area C, South Okanagan and Similkameen.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunt Map: Layers for a quail trip</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"360\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"28\" y=\"47\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"56\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">California quail habitat (60%)</text>\n<rect x=\"24\" y=\"74\" width=\"352\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e4472b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"32\" y=\"81\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#e4472b\"/>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"95\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Private land: ask first</text>\n<rect x=\"28\" y=\"108\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#78909c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"36\" y=\"115\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#78909c\"/>\n<text x=\"64\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">City and town limits: bylaws</text>\n<rect x=\"32\" y=\"142\" width=\"336\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8e5bb5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"149\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8e5bb5\"/>\n<text x=\"68\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Reserves: permission from the Nation</text>\n<rect x=\"36\" y=\"176\" width=\"328\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#3f8f3a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"44\" y=\"183\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#3f8f3a\"/>\n<text x=\"72\" y=\"197\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Parks and protected areas</text>\n<rect x=\"40\" y=\"210\" width=\"320\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#6b8e23\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"48\" y=\"217\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#6b8e23\"/>\n<text x=\"76\" y=\"231\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wildlife Management Areas</text>\n<rect x=\"44\" y=\"244\" width=\"312\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"52\" y=\"251\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"265\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Management Units (MU)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Download area C first (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Turn on: California quail habitat, Private land, City and town limits (Tip).</li><li>Then Reserves, Parks and protected areas, Management Units (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to use the layers</summary><ul><li>Open the <a href=\"#/map\">Hunt Map</a> and tap <strong>Layers</strong>.</li><li>\"California quail habitat (no migration)\": low Bunchgrass and Ponderosa Pine country near farms and brushy creeks, all year. General pattern (60%, app layer note). Loaded for areas C and D.</li><li>\"Private land\": you need the owner's permission. Not every parcel is fenced or signed (90%, app layer note).</li><li>\"City and town limits\": most ban shooting inside their limits by bylaw (95% for the boundaries; bylaws in chapter 9).</li><li>\"Reserves\": hunting needs permission from the Nation <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>\"Parks and protected areas\", \"Wildlife Management Areas\", \"Management Units\", \"Management Unit numbers\": rules differ by place <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Download area C, \"South Okanagan and Similkameen (quail trip)\", before you go: phone signal is patchy (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Four terrain tools for birds</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map terrain tool frame: Slope steepness colours the ground by angle. Gentle valley floor and benches suit quail and Huns. Steep slopes of 30 to 45 degrees with rock suit chukar. Tip: use it to find chukar ground and to avoid slopes too steep to walk safely.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Terrain tools: Slope steepness</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"360\" height=\"190\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<path d=\"M20 230 L120 230 L180 200 L240 130 L300 70 L380 60 L380 230 Z\" fill=\"#cfe3b0\"/>\n<path d=\"M180 200 L240 130 L260 140 L200 205 Z\" fill=\"#f2c14e\"/>\n<path d=\"M240 130 L300 70 L320 80 L260 140 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">gentle</text>\n<text x=\"212\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">15 to 25°</text>\n<text x=\"350\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30 to 45°</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(80 196) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(300 110) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#b9a88a\"/><path d=\"M-20 -2 L-30 -4 L-28 5 Z\" fill=\"#8b6f4a\"/><path d=\"M-8 -6 v12 M-3 -7 v13 M2 -7 v13 M7 -6 v12\" stroke=\"#2f2f2f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9fa4a8\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 q6 -2 13 2 q-4 10 -11 10\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"#f3ead8\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"-15\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M26 -14 l5 1 l-5 3 Z\" fill=\"#d23b2a\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 8 M9 13 l2 8\" stroke=\"#d23b2a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"240\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Gentle benches: quail, Huns</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Steep and rocky: chukar (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Slope steepness: gentle for quail, steep for chukar.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map terrain tool frame: Slope direction shows which way each slope faces. South facing slopes warm first and shed snow first. Washington Fish and Wildlife says chukar may roost on warmer south facing slopes on cold early season nights and gather where snow is thin, 75 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Terrain tools: Slope direction</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"360\" height=\"190\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"135\" r=\"80\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 135 L144 192 A80 80 0 0 0 256 192 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".8\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 135 L144 78 A80 80 0 0 1 256 78 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">N: cold, snow stays</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">S: warm, melts first</text>\n<text x=\"60\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">W</text>\n<text x=\"340\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">E</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"240\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cold morning: chukar on south slopes</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snow: birds on the bare patches (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Slope direction: south slopes warm and melt first.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map terrain tool frame: What can I see from here shows the ground in view from one spot. Use it to pick a glassing point over a chukar slope, then plan a stalk from above. Washington Fish and Wildlife suggests glassing distant slopes for feeding or roosting chukar, 75 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Terrain tools: What can I see</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"360\" height=\"190\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<path d=\"M20 230 L200 230 L380 80 L380 230 Z\" fill=\"#cfe3b0\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(60 200)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">glass</text></g>\n<path d=\"M60 200 L380 90 L380 200 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".25\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(300 140) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#b9a88a\"/><path d=\"M-20 -2 L-30 -4 L-28 5 Z\" fill=\"#8b6f4a\"/><path d=\"M-8 -6 v12 M-3 -7 v13 M2 -7 v13 M7 -6 v12\" stroke=\"#2f2f2f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9fa4a8\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 q6 -2 13 2 q-4 10 -11 10\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"#f3ead8\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"-15\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M26 -14 l5 1 l-5 3 Z\" fill=\"#d23b2a\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 8 M9 13 l2 8\" stroke=\"#d23b2a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">in view</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"240\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pick a spot that sees the whole slope</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Glass for chukar, then stalk from above (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> What can I see: pick a spot to glass a slope.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hunt Map terrain tool frame: Sun and shade lights the terrain from the real sun position for a time today. Chukar spend the hottest part of the day in shady cover, US Forest Service FEIS, 80 percent. Tip: for quail, check which brushy edges get the first morning sun.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Terrain tools: Sun and shade</text>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"40\" width=\"360\" height=\"190\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"70\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#f2c14e\"/>\n<path d=\"M20 230 L150 110 L280 230 Z\" fill=\"#cfe3b0\"/>\n<path d=\"M20 230 L150 110 L150 230 Z\" fill=\"#6f7f5a\"/>\n<text x=\"85\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">shade</text>\n<text x=\"215\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">sun</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"240\" width=\"380\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Midday: chukar in shade (80%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: quail on the sunny edges (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Sun and shade: shady slopes at midday, sunny edges at dawn.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Tap <strong>Terrain tools</strong> on the right of the Hunt Map <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Slope, direction, view and sun all work offline in downloaded areas <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: terrain tools in full</summary><ul><li>The Terrain sheet has four tiles: Slope steepness, Slope direction, What can I see, Sun and shade (95%, the app).</li><li>Slope steepness colours ground by angle, from gentle to over 45°. Chukar like steep slopes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>; stay off slopes you cannot walk safely (Tip).</li><li>Slope direction: on cold early season nights chukar may roost on warmer south facing slopes; later they gather where snow is thin (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife).</li><li>What can I see from here: find a glassing point over a chukar face, glass for feeding birds, then plan a stalk from above <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Sun and shade: lights the terrain for a time today and shows sunrise and sunset. Chukar sit in shade in the heat of the day <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. For quail, look for brushy edges that catch the first sun (Tip).</li><li>Lessons: <a href=\"#/s/maps-terrain\">Maps 1: reading terrain</a> and <a href=\"#/s/map-scouting\">Map scouting from home</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cross section of a South Okanagan valley side from the lake up to the pine. Riparian brush by the lake and orchard edges: quail. Brushy draws on the lower benches: quail. Farm benches and stubble: maybe gray partridge. Steep rock and cheatgrass slopes: chukar. Open pine above: few quail. Quail breed mostly from 250 to 500 metres and rarely above 750 metres, BC Breeding Bird Atlas, 85 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Valley cross section: who lives where</text>\n<path d=\"M0 250 L60 250 L90 236 L150 232 L190 210 L240 200 L270 150 L300 110 L330 90 L400 70 L400 270 L0 270 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"244\" width=\"58\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"28\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">lake</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"78\" cy=\"238\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"170\" cy=\"214\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g fill=\"#3f7f3a\"><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"226\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"128\" cy=\"225\" r=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"146\" cy=\"224\" r=\"7\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M270 150 l10 -6 l8 4 l-6 8 Z M296 116 l9 -5 l7 3 l-5 7 Z\" fill=\"#9a8f80\"/>\n<g fill=\"#556b2f\"><path d=\"M345 86 l8 -22 l8 22 Z\"/><path d=\"M372 78 l8 -22 l8 22 Z\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(84 222) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(172 198) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(286 134) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#b9a88a\"/><path d=\"M-20 -2 L-30 -4 L-28 5 Z\" fill=\"#8b6f4a\"/><path d=\"M-8 -6 v12 M-3 -7 v13 M2 -7 v13 M7 -6 v12\" stroke=\"#2f2f2f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#9fa4a8\"/><path d=\"M12 -15 q6 -2 13 2 q-4 10 -11 10\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"#f3ead8\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"-15\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M26 -14 l5 1 l-5 3 Z\" fill=\"#d23b2a\"/><path d=\"M2 13 l-2 8 M9 13 l2 8\" stroke=\"#d23b2a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g>\n<g transform=\"translate(225 190) scale(0.5 0.5)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">riparian</text>\n<text x=\"80\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">QUAIL</text>\n<text x=\"128\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">orchard</text>\n<text x=\"175\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">brushy draw</text>\n<text x=\"225\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Huns?</text>\n<text x=\"240\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">CHUKAR</text>\n<text x=\"258\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">rock + cheatgrass</text>\n<text x=\"370\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">pine</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"272\" width=\"380\" height=\"24\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail: mostly 250 to 500 m (85%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Brush by the food, water near by; quail on the low ground, chukar up high.\" (Tip)</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> \"250, 500, 750\": common from 250 to 500 m, rare above 750 m <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Map hook:</strong> \"Orange, red, grey\": quail habitat, private land, town limits. Three layers before every trip (Tip).</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule (opinion):</strong> \"Hunt the edges, not the middle.\" From the app's habitat tour Grandpa's rule (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>BC Breeding Bird Atlas, California habitat records, Washington Fish and Wildlife, Audubon, FEIS, BC Outdoors, app layers and Rule Book. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.birdatlas.bc.ca/accounts/speciesaccount.jsp?sp=CAQU&amp;lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Breeding Bird Atlas, California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: elevation, zones, habitat <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://ncrcd.specialdistrict.org/files/b900df31f/California-Quail-info.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">California Wildlife Habitat Relationships: California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68963\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Washington Fish and Wildlife: quail</a>, <a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68922\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chukar</a> and <a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68921\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gray partridge</a> hunting pages, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/chukar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Audubon field guide: chukar</a> and <a href=\"https://www.audubon.org/field-guide/bird/gray-partridge\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gray partridge</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.fs.usda.gov/database/feis/animals/bird/alch/all.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">US Forest Service FEIS: chukar</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bcoutdoorsmagazine.com/chukar-asian-partridge-made-a-home-for-itself-in-bc/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Outdoors: chukar in BC (Harris 2019)</a> and <a href=\"https://www.bcoutdoorsmagazine.com/?p=9278\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">California quail (Harris 2021)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>App: Hunt Map layer manifest (data/layers/manifest.json, updated 2026-10-11) and terrain tools; migration data (data/migration.json) (60 to 95% as marked).</li><li>Rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Rule Book, Region 8</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-3\">Region 3</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-2\">Region 2</a>, synopsis 2 October 2026 edition (97 to 99%). Town to MU table from the <a href=\"#/s/local-okanagan\">Okanagan trip plan</a> (80 to 90%).</li><li>Photos: Wikimedia Commons, credits under each photo.</li></ul></details>"]